## Completion Notes (2025-02-24)

### Changes Made

1. Modified `update-azerothcore` function:
   - Added `--force` flag support
   - Added git fetch + HEAD comparison before pulling
   - Only rebuilds if remote changes exist OR --force is used
   - Added source directory validation
   - Added Lua symlink setup (previously only in install)
   - Improved user feedback messages

2. Removed deprecated `scripts/update-2`:
   - All functionality now in main `scripts/azerothcore`
   - Old script had hardcoded paths to `/home/ritz/games/azeroth-core/`

### Command Behavior

| Scenario | Without --force | With --force |
|----------|-----------------|--------------|
| Remote has changes | Pull + rebuild | Pull + rebuild |
| No remote changes | Skip rebuild | Rebuild anyway |
| First build (no binaries) | Skip rebuild | Rebuild |

### Usage Examples

```bash
# Check for updates and rebuild only if needed
MAKE_JOBS=8 source scripts/azerothcore && azerothcore update

# Force rebuild (e.g., first compile, or after local changes)
MAKE_JOBS=8 source scripts/azerothcore && azerothcore update --force
```
